  "projected_peak_bytes": 536870912,
  "rule": "Before each launch a fresh lane scan (native solver/checker processes plus python processes whose cwd or argv lies in the lane or a review/moqls8-* desk, excluding this desk's driver and children; python counts as busy if its CPU use over a 2 s libproc window is >= 50%; lane RSS conservatively includes every such python, busy or not) and a fresh statvfs: launch only if lane busy + 2 <= 4, lane RSS (all other lane processes, a worker GB pipeline included) + max(fresh measured desk RSS, projected; an unreadable desk RSS refuses) <= 11 GiB (parent M8 lane escalation b9886e24...09ec: one GA + one GB pipeline) and free >= 12,200,000,000 + 10 MiB. Stricter than the brief: two consecutive passing checks 60 s apart are required, so a launch never rides a transient gap of the priority worker pipeline. Otherwise sleep 60 s and re-check; total gate wait per run bounded by 6 h, then stop and report deferral. No launch at or after 2026-10-18 17:29:00 PDT (host clock; 60 s margin before the 17:30 cutoff). Formula and leaf launches additionally need the parent disk monitor (review/disk-monitor-v1-20261018T0722-to-1810.jsonl, 10 s cadence; rule amended by the parent at 07:32 PDT) to show, from complete JSON lines with tz-aware strictly increasing timestamps: last sample 0 <= age <= 30 s with free >= 13,500,000,000 + 10 MiB, >= 25 samples spanning >= 290 s within the last 300 s, and a max peak-to-later free drop over that window <= max(300,000,000, (free_last - 13,500,000,000) / 12); a malformed complete line, an absent, unreadable or stale monitor refuses the launch (fail closed); the rule and a fresh statvfs are re-read at the launch decision. Controls keep the plain fresh gate. Any recorded helper survivor refuses every launch. Projected peak = formulas: max(1.5 x worker aggregate peak of the formula's source template leaf (the worker's 900 s attempt; no worker run of a strengthened formula exists), 4.6 GiB); leaves (the v2 rule): max(1.5 x worker aggregate peak of the leaf, 1.3 GiB for P0-B4 and P0-B5, else 4.6 GiB); self-tests 512 MiB.",
